bot_last_message:
For the first visible exercise, electrons are accelerated through a potential difference of \(30\,\text{kV}\).

The maximum energy of an electron becomes the energy of the highest-frequency X-ray photon:

\[
eV=h\nu_{\max}
\]

Using \(e=1.6\times10^{-19}\,\text{C}\), \(V=30\times10^3\,\text{V}\), and \(h=6.626\times10^{-34}\,\text{J·s}\):

\[
\nu_{\max}
=\frac{eV}{h}
=\frac{(1.6\times10^{-19})(30\times10^3)}
{6.626\times10^{-34}}
\]

\[
\boxed{\nu_{\max}\approx 7.25\times10^{18}\,\text{Hz}}
\]

The corresponding minimum wavelength is

\[
\lambda_{\min}=\frac{c}{\nu_{\max}}
\]

\[
\lambda_{\min}
=\frac{3.0\times10^8}{7.25\times10^{18}}
\]

\[
\boxed{\lambda_{\min}\approx 4.14\times10^{-11}\,\text{m}}
\]

or

\[
\boxed{\lambda_{\min}\approx 0.0414\,\text{nm}}
\]

